WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.632
A syrup might look sound and change before it was used.

00:00:04.632 --> 00:00:07.293
Sugar could crystallize. Its consistency could shift.

00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:10.714
The jar revealed little about the work that produced

00:00:10.714 --> 00:00:11.095
it.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.023
I found that problem in thirteenth-century

00:00:15.023 --> 00:00:17.597
pharmaceutical writing. Recipes were not simply

00:00:17.597 --> 00:00:21.028
inventories of ingredients. They also described what to

00:00:21.028 --> 00:00:24.459
do to the materials, and when to stop.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:30.027
In Minhāj al-dukkān, the discussion of syrups begins

00:00:30.027 --> 00:00:34.051
with julāb, sugar and rose water. The base was

00:00:34.051 --> 00:00:36.734
familiar; producing a dependable preparation was

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:37.628
another matter.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:45.094
Heat, skimming, and straining belong to the procedure.

00:00:45.094 --> 00:00:48.738
Qiwām, the right consistency, required judgment by the

00:00:48.738 --> 00:00:51.471
maker rather than a numerical display.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.058
The text even discusses remedies when a syrup

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:01.214
crystallizes. A preparation does not become reliable

00:01:01.214 --> 00:01:04.371
merely because the fire has been extinguished.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.398
A Cairo Genizah prescription names powdered ingredients

00:01:12.398 --> 00:01:16.609
to be worked with rose syrup. It records what was

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:20.399
requested. It cannot show us what a patient eventually

00:01:20.399 --> 00:01:20.820
received.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:27.201
A missing ingredient introduced a second decision. Some

00:01:27.201 --> 00:01:30.014
manuals permitted substitution under conditions. That

00:01:30.014 --> 00:01:34.234
was a practical response to scarcity, not permission to

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:34.703
deceive.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:40.551
Market inspectors worried about false measures and

00:01:40.551 --> 00:01:44.096
concealed practices. Trust could not rest entirely on

00:01:44.096 --> 00:01:47.197
the buyer's ability to examine a jar.

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:53.206
The surviving texts preserve this work of making

00:01:53.206 --> 00:01:56.651
medicine dependable, and the limits of what we can know

00:01:56.651 --> 00:01:57.340
about it.
